(* fs-records-b2s UKSr, security result, (K_s, K_r, T_max) = (2, 3, 2), any
   Beacon pins: record identity agreement.  A Server object never accepts a
   fresh record that a Beacon pinning its key allocated from a peer
   installed for another identity: the identity of the accepting peer is
   that of the sending Beacon.  Run in the process in which the attacker
   chooses the pinned Server key and Server ID of every Beacon, so Beacons
   that pin an attacker key, whose fresh records the attacker reads
   (PINREAD), run alongside.  Also the target of the control C-UKS. *)
query s: bitstring, b1: bitstring, b2: bitstring, kid1: key_id, kid2: key_id, root1: bitstring,
      root2: bitstring, t1: nat, t2: nat, m: bitstring;
  event(FsReceived(beacon_to_server(), s, b1, kid1, root1, t1, m))
  && event(FsSent(beacon_to_server(), s, b2, kid2, root2, t2, m))
  ==> b1 = b2.

process FsRecordsB2sMainAnyPin()
